Valid: true. Duplicate SHA256 15001657e365a127fcb4a5722747879bd6ef570a5c8008804edf285cf0c38168.
All eight inherited A56 single-flip-insensitive positions remained individually collapse-preserving in both U_A0/U_A25:
103,105,106,111,117,121,123,125.
Seven of 28 pair flips abolished collapse identically in both modes:
(103,111),(105,111),(105,117),(106,111),(106,117),(117,123),(121,123).
Interpretation: the A56-resistant positions are not all noncausal. Several carry redundant pairwise interactions: neither member alone changes the phenotype, but specific pairs do.
Plain speak: some apparently harmless stream positions are backups for one another. Change either one alone and failure still happens; change the right two together and failure disappears.
Next: test exactly the triples among the eight resistant positions whose three constituent pairs were all pairwise robust. This isolates genuinely third-order interactions without retesting triples already containing a known causal pair.
